    "text": "{\"anomaly_detected\": true, \"confidence\": 0.5, \"anomalies\": [{\"category\": \"bridged_nets\", \"components\": [\"D30\", \"R60\"], \"pins\": [\"D30.2\", \"D30.4\", \"R60.2\"], \"nets\": [\"ESTOP_OUT\", \"Net-(D30-K2)\"], \"observed\": \"R60 (130R) connects Net-(D30-K2), which is D30 pin 2 (K2), to ESTOP_OUT. D30 pin 4 (A2) is also on ESTOP_OUT. Both terminals of the second LED half of D30 therefore sit on the same net, so that LED can never be forward-biased. The mirror-image half, D30 pin 1 (K1) through R59 to GND with pin 3 (A1) on the LED supply net, has its resistor returned to GND.\", \"expected\": \"By symmetry with the K1/R59 half, R60 should return the K2 cathode to GND, with only the anode A2 driven by ESTOP_OUT. The ESTOP_OUT indicator LED should then be lit when ESTOP_OUT is asserted.\", \"evidence\": [{\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"Net-(D30-K2) : D30.2(K2,input) R60.1(passive)\"}, {\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"ESTOP_OUT : D30.4(A2,input) J13.6(Pin_6,passive) J2.6(Pin_6,passive) R60.2(passive) U36.4(Y,output)\"}, {\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"Net-(D30-K1) : D30.1(K1,input) R59.1(passive)\"}, {\"source\": \"spice\", \"quote\": \"R60 Net-_D30-K2_ ESTOP_OUT 130\"}], \"impact\": \"The ESTOP_OUT indicator LED (D30 second half) never lights, so the e-stop status indicator is non-functional. R60 also loads the ESTOP_OUT line that is shared with the CAN connectors J2 and J13 without providing the intended return path.\", \"confidence\": 0.5}], \"summary\": \"In the D30 dual LED, R60 returns the K2 cathode to ESTOP_OUT rather than GND, so both ends of that LED sit on the same net. This is inconsistent with the K1/R59 half, which returns to GND, and disables the e-stop indicator.\"}",
